WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.353
Authorization is where hand-typed
settings usually drift,

2
00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:05.712
so the builder writes
it from the registry.

3
00:00:05.712 --> 00:00:09.487
On the Logic App, shared access
signatures are switched off and

4
00:00:09.487 --> 00:00:13.551
Learn's proof-of-possession policy
goes in with Learn's exact claims.

5
00:00:13.551 --> 00:00:17.808
On the extension, the code asks for
proof-of-possession, following Learn's

6
00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:22.350
security guidance even though one example
still shows the older bearer type.

7
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.494
And the identity stays small: because
the Logic App is an authorized

8
00:00:26.494 --> 00:00:30.637
app on the extension, it can call
back with no Graph permission at all.

9
00:00:30.637 --> 00:00:34.099
The tenant-wide alternative is
what Learn advises against.

10
00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:35.520
Now, who does this work?
